# Borders - Essential Rules

## ✅ ALWAYS Use Smart Border Utility Classes

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Use our custom border utilities
<div className="bg-card p-4 rounded-lg border-default">
<div className="border-thick">
<div className="border-dashed">
<div className="border-top-default">
```

## ⚠️ Why Not Tailwind Border Classes

Tailwind v4's `border` class sets `border-width: 0px` by default, making borders invisible.

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - No visible border
<div className="border border-border">

// ✅ CORRECT - Use our utility classes
<div className="border-default">
```

## 🎯 Common Border Patterns

```tsx
// Standard border
className = "border-default";

// Thick border
className = "border-thick";

// Dashed border
className = "border-dashed";

// Top border only
className = "border-top-default";

// Bottom border only
className = "border-bottom-default";

// Left border only
className = "border-left-default";

// Right border only
className = "border-right-default";
```

## 🎯 Key Rule

**Use our smart border utility classes** instead of Tailwind border classes or inline styles.

